# A2/A2.1/A2_08_character_and_comparison.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L6 (Part 1) a21convlotsmanmeli.pdf" + "L6 (Part 2) a21lotsmanmeli.pdf"
# (A2.1, Lektioun 6). Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered
# pages, then every lemma verified against LOD.
# Grammar focus (all three from this deck):
#   - relative pronouns dee(n) m / déi f+pl / dat n, which send the verb to the end
#   - possessive pronouns, whose form depends on the gender of the POSSESSED noun
#     (mäi Brudder m / meng Schwëster f / mäi Kand n)
#   - the comparative: méi + adjective + wéi, with gutt -> besser as the exception
# ⚠️ The source handout writes "diskussiounsfreedeg"; LOD returns found: 0 and
# suggests "diskussiounsbereet". Kept the handout form out of the @word list and
# used the LOD-verified adjectives instead, so nothing unverifiable is taught.

@lesson A2.08 "Character & Comparison"

# --- Character traits ---
@word de Charakter = the character
@word éiergäizeg = ambitious
@word oppen = open-minded
@word arrogant = arrogant
@word gedëlleg = patient
@word ausgeglach = balanced
@word jalous = jealous
@word gescheit = clever
@word domm = stupid
@word liddereg = lazy
@word kannereg = childish
@word guttmiddeg = good-natured
@word langweileg = boring
@word komplizéiert = complicated
@word sympathesch = likeable
@word seriö = serious
@word flott = nice
@word rosen = angry
@word traureg = sad
@word déierefrëndlech = animal-friendly

# --- Appearance ---
@word d'Glatz = the bald head
@word d'Krausel = the curl
@word fierwen = to dye
@word gefierft = dyed
@word d'Bezéiung = the relationship

# --- Comparison ---
@word méi = more
@word besser = better
@word am beschten = the best
@word staark = strong
@word schwaach = weak

@sentence
@lu Wéi ass säin Charakter?
@en What is his character like?
@distractor-en name
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu Numm
@distractor-lu Wou

@sentence
@lu Verkeefer musse frëndlech sinn.
@en Salespeople have to be friendly.
@distractor-en arrogant
@distractor-en lazy
@distractor-lu arrogant
@distractor-lu liddereg

@sentence
@lu Ech sinn eng éiergäizeg Persoun.
@en I am an ambitious person.
@distractor-en lazy
@distractor-en boring
@distractor-lu liddereg
@distractor-lu langweileg

@sentence
@lu Meng Fra ass eng oppen Persoun.
@en My wife is an open-minded person.
@distractor-en arrogant
@distractor-en complicated
@distractor-lu arrogant
@distractor-lu komplizéiert

@sentence
@lu Hie gesäit rosen aus.
@en He looks angry.
@distractor-en sad
@distractor-en tired
@distractor-lu traureg
@distractor-lu midd

@sentence
@lu Ass eppes geschitt?
@en Did something happen?
@distractor-en nothing
@distractor-en who
@distractor-lu näischt
@distractor-lu Wien

@sentence
@lu Ech sinn absolut net liddereg.
@en I am absolutely not lazy.
@distractor-en ambitious
@distractor-en sad
@distractor-lu éiergäizeg
@distractor-lu traureg

@sentence
@lu Hien ass sou kannereg.
@en He is so childish.
@distractor-en clever
@distractor-en patient
@distractor-lu gescheit
@distractor-lu gedëlleg

@sentence
@lu Hie gesäit mam Brëll gescheit aus.
@en He looks clever with the glasses.
@distractor-en stupid
@distractor-en sad
@distractor-lu domm
@distractor-lu traureg

@sentence
@lu Gëss du séier jalous?
@en Do you get jealous quickly?
@distractor-en angry
@distractor-en patient
@distractor-lu rosen
@distractor-lu gedëlleg

@sentence
@lu Meng Schwëster ass ganz ausgeglach.
@en My sister is very balanced.
@distractor-en complicated
@distractor-en jealous
@distractor-lu komplizéiert
@distractor-lu jalous

@sentence
@lu Meng Mamm ass ganz déierefrëndlech.
@en My mother is very animal-friendly.
@distractor-en arrogant
@distractor-en lazy
@distractor-lu arrogant
@distractor-lu liddereg

@sentence
@lu Mäi Chef ass frëndlech a gedëlleg.
@en My boss is friendly and patient.
@distractor-en arrogant
@distractor-en boring
@distractor-lu arrogant
@distractor-lu langweileg

@sentence
@lu Wéi heescht déi nei Cheffin?
@en What is the new boss called?
@distractor-en old
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu al
@distractor-lu Wou

@sentence
@lu Kenns du schonn déi nei Noperen?
@en Do you already know the new neighbours?
@distractor-en old
@distractor-en when
@distractor-lu al
@distractor-lu Wéini

@sentence
@lu Déi éischt Klass ass komplett voll.
@en The first class is completely full.
@distractor-en empty
@distractor-en second
@distractor-lu eidel
@distractor-lu zweet

@sentence
@lu Meng Frëndin huet hir Hoer gefierft.
@en My girlfriend dyed her hair.
@distractor-en cut
@distractor-en curl
@distractor-lu geschnidden
@distractor-lu Krausel

@sentence
@lu Mäi Brudder huet eng Glatz.
@en My brother has a bald head.
@distractor-en glasses
@distractor-en curl
@distractor-lu Brëll
@distractor-lu Krausel

@sentence
@lu Ech si méi seriö wéi mäi Partner.
@en I am more serious than my partner.
@distractor-en less
@distractor-en childish
@distractor-lu manner
@distractor-lu kannereg

@sentence
@lu Mäi Partner ass méi kannereg wéi ech.
@en My partner is more childish than me.
@distractor-en serious
@distractor-en less
@distractor-lu seriö
@distractor-lu manner

@sentence
@lu En Hond ass méi gescheit wéi eng Kaz.
@en A dog is more clever than a cat.
@distractor-en stupid
@distractor-en less
@distractor-lu domm
@distractor-lu manner

@sentence
@lu Dat lescht Joer war méi kal wéi dëst Joer.
@en Last year was colder than this year.
@distractor-en warm
@distractor-en next
@distractor-lu waarm
@distractor-lu nächst

@sentence
@lu Mäi Brudder ass méi staark wéi ech.
@en My brother is stronger than me.
@distractor-en weak
@distractor-en less
@distractor-lu schwaach
@distractor-lu manner

@sentence
@lu Dëse Kaffi ass besser wéi deen aneren.
@en This coffee is better than the other one.
@distractor-en worse
@distractor-en more
@distractor-lu schlechter
@distractor-lu méi

@sentence
@lu Meng Bezéiung mat mengem Brudder ass gutt.
@en My relationship with my brother is good.
@distractor-en bad
@distractor-en sister
@distractor-lu schlecht
@distractor-lu Schwëster

@sentence
@lu Hatt schwätzt gär iwwer komplizéiert Themen.
@en She likes talking about complicated topics.
@distractor-en boring
@distractor-en never
@distractor-lu langweileg
@distractor-lu ni

@sentence
@lu Wann ech midd sinn, sinn ech liddereg.
@en When I am tired, I am lazy.
@distractor-en strong
@distractor-en ambitious
@distractor-lu staark
@distractor-lu éiergäizeg

@sentence
@lu Ech fannen dëse Film langweileg.
@en I find this film boring.
@distractor-en nice
@distractor-en clever
@distractor-lu flott
@distractor-lu gescheit

@sentence
@lu Meng Noperen si ganz flott.
@en My neighbours are very nice.
@distractor-en arrogant
@distractor-en boring
@distractor-lu arrogant
@distractor-lu langweileg

@sentence
@lu Firwat bass du traureg?
@en Why are you sad?
@distractor-en angry
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu rosen
@distractor-lu Wou

# --- @fill: relative pronouns ------------------------------------------------
# Chosen by the gender of the noun they refer back to, and they send the verb to
# the end of the clause. The wrong-gender pronoun is the distractor.

@fill
@lu Dat ass de Mann, [deen] ech gutt kennen.
@en That is the man [whom] I know well.
@distractor-lu déi
@distractor-lu dat
@distractor-lu wien
@distractor-en which
@distractor-en whose
@distractor-en what

@fill
@lu Dat ass d'Fra, [déi] ëmmer frëndlech ass.
@en That is the woman [who] is always friendly.
@distractor-lu deen
@distractor-lu dat
@distractor-lu wien
@distractor-en whom
@distractor-en whose
@distractor-en what

@fill
@lu E Kand, [dat] gär schwammt, ass gesond.
@en A child [which] likes swimming is healthy.
@distractor-lu deen
@distractor-lu déi
@distractor-lu wien
@distractor-en who
@distractor-en whose
@distractor-en what

@fill
@lu Ech sichen e Partner, [deen] net jalous gëtt.
@en I am looking for a partner [who] does not get jealous.
@distractor-lu déi
@distractor-lu dat
@distractor-lu wien
@distractor-en whose
@distractor-en which
@distractor-en what

@fill
@lu Si toleréiert Leit, [déi] sech arrogant behuelen.
@en She tolerates people [who] behave arrogantly.
@distractor-lu deen
@distractor-lu dat
@distractor-lu wien
@distractor-en whose
@distractor-en whom
@distractor-en what

# --- @fill: possessive pronouns ----------------------------------------------
# The form depends on the gender of the POSSESSED noun, not the owner:
# mäi Brudder (m) / meng Schwëster (f) / mäi Kand (n) / meng Kanner (pl).

@fill
@lu [Mäi] Brudder ass ganz éiergäizeg.
@en [My] brother is very ambitious.
@distractor-lu Meng
@distractor-lu Mäin
@distractor-lu Eis
@distractor-en Our
@distractor-en Your
@distractor-en Their

@fill
@lu [Meng] Schwëster ass ganz sympathesch.
@en [My] sister is very likeable.
@distractor-lu Mäi
@distractor-lu Mäin
@distractor-lu Eis
@distractor-en Our
@distractor-en Your
@distractor-en Their

@fill
@lu Ass dat [hire] Frënd?
@en Is that [her] friend?
@distractor-lu hir
@distractor-lu hiert
@distractor-lu eise
@distractor-en our
@distractor-en your
@distractor-en their

@fill
@lu Wéi ass [Ären] Numm?
@en What is [your] name?
@distractor-lu Är
@distractor-lu Äert
@distractor-lu Eise
@distractor-en our
@distractor-en her
@distractor-en their

@fill
@lu [Eise] Hond huet Kanner gär.
@en [Our] dog likes children.
@distractor-lu Eis
@distractor-lu Eist
@distractor-lu Hir
@distractor-en Her
@distractor-en Your
@distractor-en Their

@fill
@lu [Säi] Papp ass ganz gedëlleg.
@en [His] dad is very patient.
@distractor-lu Seng
@distractor-lu Säin
@distractor-lu Hir
@distractor-en Her
@distractor-en Our
@distractor-en Their

# --- @fill: the comparative --------------------------------------------------
# méi + adjective + wéi. `gutt` is irregular: besser, never "méi gutt".

@fill
@lu Meng Schwëster ass [méi] gedëlleg wéi ech.
@en My sister is [more] patient than me.
@distractor-lu manner
@distractor-lu ganz
@distractor-lu esou
@distractor-en less
@distractor-en very
@distractor-en as

@fill
@lu E Mupp ass méi flott [wéi] eng Kaz.
@en A dog is nicer [than] a cat.
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu well
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-en when
@distractor-en because
@distractor-en and

@fill
@lu Dëse Téi ass [besser] wéi deen aneren.
@en This tea is [better] than the other one.
@distractor-lu gutt
@distractor-lu gudden
@distractor-lu schlecht
@distractor-en good
@distractor-en best
@distractor-en bad

@fill
@lu Dat ass [am] beschten fir meng Gesondheet.
@en That is [the] best for my health.
@distractor-lu méi
@distractor-lu manner
@distractor-lu wéi
@distractor-en more
@distractor-en less
@distractor-en than

# --- @fill: conjunctions with the verb at the end -----------------------------

@fill
@lu Ech maache Sport, [obwuel] ech midd sinn.
@en I do sport [although] I am tired.
@distractor-lu well
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu ob
@distractor-en because
@distractor-en if
@distractor-en whether

@fill
@lu Hatt ass frou, [well] hatt eng gutt Bezéiung huet.
@en She is happy [because] she has a good relationship.
@distractor-lu obwuel
@distractor-lu wann
@distractor-lu ob
@distractor-en although
@distractor-en if
@distractor-en whether

@fill
@lu Ech denken, [datt] mäi Chef gedëlleg ass.
@en I think [that] my boss is patient.
@distractor-lu well
@distractor-lu obwuel
@distractor-lu ob
@distractor-en because
@distractor-en although
@distractor-en whether

